  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Four gates on the coach's call",
  "description": "Set up four gates of two cones each, one in each corner of the area, and name them: A and B at the top, C and D at the bottom. Every player has a ball and skates freely in the middle.\n\nThe coach calls a gate. Everyone carries the ball there, skates through and round the gate, and heads back towards the middle. Before they get there the coach calls the next gate. Since everyone is heading for the same gate at once, the players must keep their heads up and see where the others are so nobody collides.\n\nVariant: call two gates in a row, let players swap balls with someone in the middle, or call a colour instead of a letter. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Heads up – look at the ice, not only at the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to the stick when it gets crowded at the gate."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Listen to the coach and change direction straight away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Use crossovers when you round the gate."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
